name 'pl-aif1-js-practice-rubric'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>A Student Reactive Logic Project</h1>

<p>Before practicing with the rubric, take a look at an actual student submission: a small app called Mood Playlist Picker. A user picks a mood, and the app shows a matching playlist and background color.</p>

<div style="background-color: #FFF8EF; border: 1px solid #F0DCC4; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p style="font-weight: 700; color: #8A4B00; margin-bottom: 8px;">STUDENT'S PSEUDOCODE</p>
<div style="font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: #5C3A00; line-height: 1.8;">
START<br>
Ask user to pick a mood (happy, chill, sad)<br>
IF mood is happy<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;show upbeat playlist<br>
IF mood is chill<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;show lofi playlist<br>
END
</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #2B2745; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p style="font-weight: 700; color: #ACA8EA; margin-bottom: 8px; font-family: system-ui;">STUDENT'S CODE (script.js)</p>
<div style="font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; color: #E4E2F8; line-height: 1.8;">
let mood = "";<br><br>
function showPlaylist() {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;if (mood === "happy") {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;playlistText.textContent = "Upbeat Anthems";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;document.body.style.backgroundColor = "#FFE3CE";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;} else if (mood === "chill") {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;playlistText.textContent = "Lo-Fi Focus";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;document.body.style.backgroundColor = "#D5EFFF";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;} else {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;playlistText.textContent = "Rainy Day Ballads";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;document.body.style.backgroundColor = "#CBD6E3";<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;}<br>
}<br><br>
happyButton.addEventListener("click", () =&gt; { mood = "happy"; showPlaylist(); });<br>
chillButton.addEventListener("click", () =&gt; { mood = "chill"; showPlaylist(); });<br>
sadButton.addEventListener("click", () =&gt; { mood = "sad"; showPlaylist(); });
</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #FFF8EF; border: 1px solid #F0DCC4; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p style="font-weight: 700; color: #8A4B00; margin-bottom: 8px;">STUDENT'S REFLECTION</p>
<p style="color: #5C3A00; font-style: italic;">"For this project I used AI to help me write the if/else code because I wasn't sure how to make the background color change. It worked pretty well after I told it what colors I wanted. I think my app turned out okay."</p>
</div>

---
<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
<iframe src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit5AIF2/mood-playlist-picker.html" width="100%" height="820" style="border:none;" title="sample student project for a mood playlist picker"></iframe>
</div>



---

<p>On the next level, you'll grade this exact project against all five rubric rows.</p>
MARKDOWN
